    "result_text": "The annotation is wired onto the generated `OwnerFieldsDto.registrationDate` field, so validation runs via the standard Bean Validation path before the controller.\n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with all three findings and refactored accordingly.\n\n**What changed:**\n1. **New constraint** \u2014 `rest/validation/RegistrationDateValidation.java` (annotation) + `RegistrationDateValidator.java` (validator). The validator mirrors `PetAgeValidator` exactly: tolerates `null`, rejects `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`.\n2. **Wiring** \u2014 added `x-field-extra-annotation` for the constraint to the `registrationDate` field in `openapi.yml`, the same way `TelephoneValidation`/`PetAgeValidation` are wired. Confirmed it propagates to the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n3. **Removed** the inline `if (suppliedDate.isAfter(...)) return BAD_REQUEST` guard from `addOwner`.\n\n**Effect on the findings:**\n- **(1) Wrong unit** \u2014 fixed; the rule now lives as a field-level constraint in the dedicated `rest/validation` package, parallel to the existing temporal constraint on pet birth dates.\n- **(2) Inconsistent error surface** \u2014 fixed for free; the failure now flows through `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`, so it returns the same structured 400 `ProblemDetail` (with `errors`/`schemaValidationErrors`) as every other input-validation failure, rather than a bare bodiless 400.\n- **(3) Overloaded method** \u2014 fixed; `addOwner` no longer carries field-sanity validation.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is intact: the future-dated `2999-01-01` payload still yields 400, an omitted date still defaults to the server date, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
